{"availability":"available","full":"supertestnet/hedgehog","name":"hedgehog","description":"A protocol for improved layer two bitcoin payments","category":"Finance","language":"HTML","stars":90,"forks":7,"created":"2024-03-23T13:24:56Z","updated":"2026-04-28T04:42:53Z","license":"CC0-1.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://supertestnet.github.io/hedgehog/","topics":[],"demo":"https://supertestnet.github.io/hedgehog/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:14:43.597Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:14:43.597Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:14:43.597Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.990Z","stars":90,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-10T13:01:15.077Z","stars":90,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-16T07:14:43.597Z","stars":90,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A protocol for improved layer two bitcoin payments","Hedgehog is a protocol for two party payment channels. Hedgehog channels are similar to lightning channels but with a few comparative benefits.","The properties mentioned above allow for an improved payment experience. Using hedgehog feels similar to using an ecash protocol like cashu or fedimint, except with no server. If you have a channel with someone, you can -- without their assistance -- create a payment for them, embed it in a piece of text (think of it like a cheque), and send it to them via email or some other communication method. Then you can go offline. When they get online, they can either accept the state change (the cheque) and update their balance without your further assistance, or they can reject it. If they accept…"],"features":["Hedgehog channels are simpler than lightning channels","State updates only require the sender to propose an update and the recipient to accept it","The recipient can wait to accept a state change til they want to propose another one"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/supertestnet/hedgehog/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"268fbdfcd811e8353dbb31ea47